  "name": "Merchant Side | Max AI: Blog | Max Copywriter Enhancements",
  "text_content": "Issue: Max Blog/Copywriter Flow Creates Too Much Friction + Misses Existing Instructions\nGoal\nI want to generate a complete blog in one go without needing multiple follow-up prompts or answering repetitive setup questions—especially when the AI already has prior instructions/context.\nCurrent Workflow Issue\nI use Max to create comparison blogs with a consistent structure and predefined requirements.\nMy standard requirements are:\nConsistent blog template:\nMain content\nSoft CTA\n5 short FAQs\nFinal thoughts section\nBlog angle:\nPosition Prosperna as the alternative/solution to the problem or comparison topic.\nHowever, Max still asks repetitive setup questions such as:\nBlog format\nWriting style\nTarget audience\nTone\nBlog length\nAfter answering these, it generates an outline but often forgets the initial instruction to integrate Prosperna into the blog, which is a key requirement.\nComparison to Claude\nIn Claude, once the prompt/context is established, it:\nGenerates the full blog directly\nFollows the expected structure consistently\nRetains the instruction to position Prosperna within the content\nUses web search to improve accuracy, credibility, and freshness of facts/statistics\nSuggestions / Feature Requests\nWeb Search Integration\nAdd a web search capability so blogs can include updated facts, statistics, and more credible information.\nPreset / Memory for Blog Preferences\nAllow users to save preset blog instructions (e.g., tone, structure, audience, CTA format, Prosperna positioning).\nThis would reduce repetitive questioning and allow faster one-shot blog generation.\nExpected Outcome\nThe goal is for Max to generate a complete, structured blog in a single prompt, while consistently following previously established blog requirements without needing repeated clarification.\n\nEncountered Problems\nBlog agent sometimes fails to call Blog_Widget_Field_Edit tool for automatic injection into frontend fields, this may be because of the agent's lack of strict instructions. Strengthening the instruction was advised\nBlog agent sometimes fails to call",
  "description": "Issue: Max Blog/Copywriter Flow Creates Too Much Friction + Misses Existing Instructions\nGoal\nI want to generate a complete blog in one go without needing multiple follow-up prompts or answering repetitive setup questions—especially when the AI already has prior instructions/context.\nCurrent Workflow Issue\nI use Max to create comparison blogs with a consistent structure and predefined requirements.\nMy standard requirements are:\nConsistent blog template:\nMain content\nSoft CTA\n5 short FAQs\nFinal thoughts section\nBlog angle:\nPosition Prosperna as the alternative/solution to the problem or comparison topic.\nHowever, Max still asks repetitive setup questions such as:\nBlog format\nWriting style\nTarget audience\nTone\nBlog length\nAfter answering these, it generates an outline but often forgets the initial instruction to integrate Prosperna into the blog, which is a key requirement.\nComparison to Claude\nIn Claude, once the prompt/context is established, it:\nGenerates the full blog directly\nFollows the expected structure consistently\nRetains the instruction to position Prosperna within the content\nUses web search to improve accuracy, credibility, and freshness of facts/statistics\nSuggestions / Feature Requests\nWeb Search Integration\nAdd a web search capability so blogs can include updated facts, statistics, and more credible information.\nPreset / Memory for Blog Preferences\nAllow users to save preset blog instructions (e.g., tone, structure, audience, CTA format, Prosperna positioning).\nThis would reduce repetitive questioning and allow faster one-shot blog generation.\nExpected Outcome\nThe goal is for Max to generate a complete, structured blog in a single prompt, while consistently following previously established blog requirements without needing repeated clarification.\n\nEncountered Problems\nBlog agent sometimes fails to call Blog_Widget_Field_Edit tool for automatic injection into frontend fields, this may be because of the agent's lack of strict instructions. Strengthening the instruction was advised\nBlog agent sometimes fails to call",
  "markdown_description": "**Issue: Max Blog/Copywriter Flow Creates Too Much Friction + Misses Existing Instructions**\n### Goal\nI want to generate a **complete blog in one go** without needing multiple follow-up prompts or answering repetitive setup questions—especially when the AI already has prior instructions/context.\n### Current Workflow Issue\nI use Max to create **comparison blogs** with a **consistent structure** and predefined requirements.\nMy standard requirements are:\n*   Consistent blog template:\n    *   Main content\n    *   Soft CTA\n    *   5 short FAQs\n    *   Final thoughts section\n*   Blog angle:\n    *   Position **Prosperna as the alternative/solution** to the problem or comparison topic.\nHowever, Max still asks repetitive setup questions such as:\n*   Blog format\n*   Writing style\n*   Target audience\n*   Tone\n*   Blog length\nAfter answering these, it generates an outline but often **forgets the initial instruction to integrate Prosperna into the blog**, which is a key requirement.\n### Comparison to Claude\nIn Claude, once the prompt/context is established, it:\n*   Generates the **full blog directly**\n*   Follows the expected structure consistently\n*   Retains the instruction to position Prosperna within the content\n*   Uses **web search** to improve accuracy, credibility, and freshness of facts/statistics\n### Suggestions / Feature Requests\n1. **Web Search Integration**\n    *   Add a web search capability so blogs can include updated facts, statistics, and more credible information.\n2. **Preset / Memory for Blog Preferences**\n    *   Allow users to save preset blog instructions (e.g., tone, structure, audience, CTA format, Prosperna positioning).\n    *   This would reduce repetitive questioning and allow faster one-shot blog generation.\n### Expected Outcome\nThe goal is for Max to generate a **complete, structured blog in a single prompt**, while consistently following previously established blog requirements without needing repeated clarification.\n\n### Encountered Problems\n*   Blog agent sometimes fails to call Blog\\_Widget\\_Field\\_Edit tool for automatic injection into frontend fields, this may be because of the agent's lack of strict instructions. Strengthening the instruction was advised\n*   Blog agent sometimes fails to call",
